description = "Minimal libretro hardware-render diagnostic core. It requests compatibility OpenGL/GLES2 hardware rendering, uses the shared libretro glsym wrapper, draws one triangle plus embedded f-6x8f FNT bitmap text through GLES2-era shaders, and submits silent audio every retro_run. Software red means HW negotiation was rejected before hardware mode. After HW negotiation succeeds, missing frontend FBO or missing context_reset is reported with a frontend OSD message plus a legal duplicate frame. GL orange/magenta/yellow means triangle bootstrap stopped after GL reached the frontend FBO, purple means triangle initialized but bitmap text setup failed, and blue with text means the triangle and text renderer initialized."
